      "message": "This doesn\u0027t address the problem I had in mind. I think you also have to revert the change that added vma-\u003eanon_vma \u003d NULL; in unlink_anon_vmas().\nYou can have a situation where thread A starts doing an SPF walk through VMA A and gets past the point of no return (where the page table lock is held), then thread B merges VMA A into an adjacent VMA B, which causes VMA A to be removed from the VMA tree and unlinked from the anon_vma.\nThe anon_vma is guaranteed to still be there; VMA B must be associated with the same anon_vma, otherwise the merge wouldn\u0027t have been possible, and VMA B still holds a reference to the anon_vma.\nBut VMA A suddenly isn\u0027t pointing to it anymore, the -\u003eanon_vma pointer was nulled out by unlink_anon_vmas().",
